sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant API@{ "type": "control" } as Dictaphone API
    participant Reencoder@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP re-encoding worker
    participant Validator@{ "type": "control" } as HTTP validation worker
    participant DB@{ "type": "database" } as PostgreSQL
    participant Queue@{ "type": "queue" } as Redis and Celery queue
    participant Backend@{ "type": "control" } as Backend worker
    participant Gateway@{ "type": "control" } as S3 egress gateway
    participant FileStore@{ "type": "database" } as File-linked object storage
    participant Summary@{ "type": "boundary" } as Summary service

    Reencoder->>API: GET /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/transcoding/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Reencoder: Job id, expires_at, source_url, destination_url, destination_headers
    Reencoder->>Gateway: Fresh attempt child: GET /proxy<br/>X-Target-URL: source_url
    Gateway->>FileStore: Allowlisted GET using original signed URL
    FileStore-->>Gateway: Source object
    Gateway-->>Reencoder: Stream source object to child
    Reencoder->>Reencoder: Child transcodes with FFmpeg
    Reencoder->>Gateway: Child: PUT /proxy with destination_headers + Content-Length<br/>X-Target-URL: destination_url
    Gateway->>FileStore: Allowlisted PUT using original signed URL
    FileStore-->>Gateway: Upload response
    Gateway-->>Reencoder: Upload response
    Reencoder->>API: POST /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/transcoding/complete<br/>id and status<br/>duration_seconds on success or error on failure
    API->>DB: Record transcoding result and duration<br/>make validation job available on success
    Validator->>API: GET /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/validation/next<br/>Bearer token
    API-->>Validator: Job id, expires_at, source_url
    Validator->>Gateway: Fresh attempt child: GET /proxy<br/>X-Target-URL: source_url
    Gateway->>FileStore: Allowlisted GET using original signed URL
    FileStore-->>Gateway: Converted audio
    Gateway-->>Validator: Stream audio to child
    Validator->>Validator: Child validates with opusinfo + opusdec
    Validator->>API: POST /api/internal/v1.0/audio-jobs/validation/complete<br/>id, status, error on failure
    API->>DB: Record successful validation attempt<br/>derived state becomes EXTRACTION_DONE<br/>Reserve or reuse unlinked PENDING transcript job<br/>link validated audio, retain language
    API->>Queue: call_transcribe_service.delay(ai_job_id)<br/>after commit, queue: dictaphone-backend
    Queue->>Backend: call_transcribe_service(ai_job_id)<br/>queue: dictaphone-backend
    Backend->>DB: Lock reserved transcription job<br/>load its language and validated audio attempt
    Note over DB,Backend: Skip submission if remote_job_id is already set or status is not PENDING.<br/>Revalidate audio availability and duration before submitting.
    Backend->>FileStore: Generate signed GET URL for derived audio
    Backend->>Summary: POST /api/v2/async-jobs/transcribe

    alt Transient submission failure and retries remain
        Summary-->>Backend: Transport error, HTTP 408, 429, or 5xx
        Backend->>DB: Keep transcription job PENDING, release lock
        Backend->>Queue: Retry call_transcribe_service(ai_job_id) with backoff<br/>same job, language, and validated audio
    else Permanent failure or retries exhausted
        Backend->>DB: Mark transcription job FAILED and release lock
    else Transcription request succeeds
        Summary-->>Backend: 200 pending and remote job id
        Backend->>DB: Save remote transcription job id and release lock
    end

    Note over Reencoder,Gateway: Gateway path shown: default in Helm, Compose, and Tilt.<br/>An empty S3_GATEWAY_URL uses direct storage transfers.

    Note over Reencoder,Validator: This sequence shows claimed tasks on the successful path.<br/>Empty queues wait and poll again, each Deployment stops new claims after 15 minutes.<br/>Attempt isolation, failure paths, deadlines, and health probes are detailed in the worker diagrams.
